WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.360
A famine.

2
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:04.640
A father has no way left
to feed his children.

3
00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:08.730
Across the street, a rich
man's store is full of bread.

4
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.390
Thomas Aquinas wrote about
exactly this kind of case.

5
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.710
So, in 1966, did Joseph Fletcher.

6
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.720
Is it ever right to
steal bread to survive,

7
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.290
or to lie to protect a friend?

8
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:25.520
In this mission, you'll test theft
and lying against natural law,

9
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:27.850
situation ethics and virtue ethics.

10
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.440
Then you'll see how 4 thinkers
explain the voice of conscience,

11
00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:34.680
and what it does after a lie.

12
00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:39.240
Your mission: compare how three
theories judge stealing and lying.
